<mjml>
  <!--
  ==========================================================================
  WEBINAR TEMPLATE — DAY 0 (ANNOUNCEMENT) — WITTY
  The first email that introduces the webinar. Works for any niche or topic.
  Pairs with the "webinar" (reminder) template in this same library.

  Placeholders are written {{LIKE_THIS}} and are replaced by the plugin.
  Mautic tokens ({contactfield=...}, {webview_url}, {unsubscribe_url}) are
  left untouched and resolved by Mautic at send time.

  HOW DAY 0 IS DIFFERENT FROM A REMINDER EMAIL
  A reminder email sells the DEADLINE ("last chance, tomorrow at 10:30").
  Day 0 has no deadline yet -- nobody is waiting for this email. So it has to
  sell the PROBLEM instead. The reader doesn't wake up wanting a webinar;
  they wake up with a frustration. Name that frustration more precisely than
  they could themselves, then position the webinar as the obvious next step.
  Practical consequences:
    - Longer body copy than a reminder. Day 0 is where you earn attention.
    - Only 2 CTAs, not 3. Pushing hard on a first touch reads as desperate.
    - No fake scarcity. Save real urgency for the reminder emails -- if you
      burn "last chance" on day 0, the sequence has nowhere left to go.
    - The goal is recognition, not pressure. The reader should think
      "this is literally my situation" before they see a single button.

  SIX RULES BEFORE YOU WRITE
  1. ONE goal: the click to the registration page. No links to your blog,
     socials, or homepage. Every extra link splits your click-through rate.
  2. ONE destination: both buttons point to the SAME URL. Only the wording
     changes.
  3. Write to ONE person. "You", never "you all".
  4. Sell the REGISTRATION, not the webinar. This email earns the click; the
     landing page does the selling.
  5. Benefits over topics. Not "we'll cover X", but "you'll leave able to do
     Y in Z minutes".
  6. Keep at least 60% real text. Image-heavy emails hit spam filters and
     show up blank for the ~40% of opens with images off.
  ==========================================================================
  -->

  <mj-head>
    <mj-style>
      @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&amp;display=swap');
      .hook { font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.4; color: #000000; }
      .h1 { font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-size: 29px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.28; letter-spacing: -0.7px; color: #000000; }
      .h2 { font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -0.5px; color: #000000; }
      .eyebrow { font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #999999; }
      .lead { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.6; color: #000000; }
      .meta { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; color: #666666; }
      .micro { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400; color: #999999; }
      .quote { font-style: italic; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.7; color: #000000; }
      .strong { font-weight: 600; }
      a { color: #000000; text-decoration: underline; }
      @media only screen and (max-width:480px) {
        .h1 { font-size: 24px !important; letter-spacing: -0.4px !important; }
        .hook { font-size: 17px !important; }
        .h2 { font-size: 21px !important; }
        .lead { font-size: 16px !important; }
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body width="640px" background-color="#ffffff">

    <!-- ====================================================================
    1. LOGO
    WHY: sender recognition in under half a second. A clean logo on white
    also signals "legitimate business email" to spam filters.
    HOW: 160-200px wide, transparent PNG, hosted on your own domain. Always
    fill in the alt text.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="36px 24px 28px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="{{LOGO_URL}}" width="180px" alt="{{BRAND_NAME}}" fluid-on-mobile="true" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section>
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    2. HERO VISUAL (GIF or image)
    WHY: on day 0 a face outperforms an abstract graphic: people register
    for people.
    HOW: 600px wide, 16:9. Descriptive alt text is mandatory. Avoid text
    baked into the image.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="28px 24px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="{{HERO_IMAGE_URL}}" width="600px" alt="{{HERO_IMAGE_ALT}}" fluid-on-mobile="true" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    3. TITLE BLOCK — THE PROMISE
    Assume 80% of readers will only read this block. Five parts, in order.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="16px 24px 0px">
      <mj-column>

        <!--
        3a. HOOK LINE (day-0 specific)
        WHY: the line a reminder email doesn't need. It buys the two seconds
        you need to earn the headline, via pattern interruption: a truth the
        reader agrees with instantly, followed by an unexpected turn.
        HOW: two short lines, 4-9 words each.
          Line 1 = a statement they nod at.
          Line 2 = the twist that makes it your subject.
        Formats that work: familiar truth + reversal ("Everyone wants X. /
        Almost nobody does Y."), insider observation, contradiction.
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="hook" align="center" padding-bottom="18px">
          {{HOOK}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        3b. HEADLINE
        WHY: names the transformation. Day 0 has no deadline to lean on, so
        the headline has to carry the value on its own.
        HOW: 6 to 14 words. Pick ONE angle: outcome, gap, or method. Be
        specific -- a number beats an adjective.
        BANNED: "Join our webinar", "Newsletter #12", "Don't miss out".
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="h1" align="center" padding-bottom="16px">
          {{HEADLINE}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        3c. SUBHEADLINE — THE QUALIFIER
        WHY: the headline claims, the subheadline makes it credible and
        filters the audience.
        HOW: one line, 6-14 words, the measurable part the headline couldn't
        fit.
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="lead" align="center" padding-bottom="14px">
          {{SUBHEADLINE}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        3d. SOCIAL PROOF
        WHY: on day 0 it's your only credibility signal -- the reader has no
        reason to trust you yet.
        HOW: one REAL number. No number yet? Use experience, or delete the
        block. Never invent one.
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="meta" align="center" padding-bottom="18px">
          {{SOCIAL_PROOF}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        3e. COST OF ENTRY
        HOW: be honest (~200 words/minute). Day 0 runs longer than a
        reminder, so 1-2 min is normal.
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="micro" align="center">
          {{READING_TIME}}
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    4. CTA #1 — FOR READERS ALREADY SOLD
    WHY: ~15% of readers are ready the moment they've read the promise.
    HOW: the line above states WHEN, factually (not pressure on day 0). The
    button label is first person ("Save my seat").
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="36px 24px 0px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-family="'Poppins', sans-serif" font-size="17px" font-weight="700" color="#000000" padding-bottom="18px">
          {{DATE_LINE}}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="{{REGISTRATION_URL}}">
          {{CTA_PRIMARY}}
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding="36px 24px 0px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    5. BODY — THE P.A.S. STRUCTURE
    Problem -> Agitation -> Solution. Name the pain before offering the
    cure -- the single highest-leverage part of a day-0 email.
    RULE: one idea per paragraph, two lines maximum.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="36px 24px 0px">
      <mj-column>

        <!--
        5a. PERSONALISED GREETING
        HOW: ALWAYS use a fallback with the pipe. Mautic syntax:
        {contactfield=firstname|there}
        -->
        <mj-text font-weight="400" padding-bottom="20px">
          Hi <span class="atwho-inserted" data-fr-verified="true">{contactfield=firstname|there}</span>,
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        5b. THE SITUATION — where the reader lives
        WHY: open in their world, not yours.
        HOW: 1-2 short paragraphs naming the specific circumstance.
        BANNED: "We're excited to invite you to..."
        -->
        <mj-text padding-bottom="14px">
          {{SITUATION}}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="20px">
          {{WHY_NOW}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        5c. THE PROBLEM — named out loud
        HOW: one sentence, slightly heavier weight. Add the absolving
        clause -- "and for good reason".
        -->
        <mj-text font-weight="400" padding-bottom="20px">
          {{PROBLEM}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        5d. VERBATIM QUOTES — the identification device
        WHY: the most powerful block in a day-0 email. Quoting your
        audience's exact words proves you've had this conversation before.
        HOW: 2 quotes, 1-2 lines each, from real sources. Keep the messy,
        spoken phrasing. Do NOT invent them in clean marketing language.
          Quote 1 -> the confusion
          Quote 2 -> the paralysis
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="quote" padding-bottom="20px">
          <p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;">💬 "{{QUOTE_1}}"</p>
          <p style="margin:0;">💬 "{{QUOTE_2}}"</p>
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        5e. AGITATION — the cost of doing nothing
        HOW: two short paragraphs. First the immediate consequence, then the
        slow one. Stay factual: exaggerated fear reads as manipulation.
        -->
        <mj-text font-weight="400" padding-bottom="12px">
          {{IMMEDIATE_COST}}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-weight="400" padding-bottom="20px">
          {{SLOW_COST}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        5f. THE PIVOT
        HOW: max 8 words. "That's exactly what we help you fix."
        -->
        <mj-text>
          {{PIVOT}}
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding="36px 24px 0px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    6. WEBINAR DETAILS — THE PROOF IT'S REAL
    WHY: the body sold the problem; this block proves the answer exists.
    Also the block scanners jump to -- must work on its own.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="36px 24px 0px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text css-class="eyebrow" padding-bottom="8px">
          Webinar details
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        6b. SESSION NAME
        HOW: keep it short, repeat the exact same name on the landing page.
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="h2" padding-bottom="8px">
          {{SESSION_NAME}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        6c. DATE & TIME
        HOW: day + date + time. Add the time zone if your list spans more
        than one. Re-check EVERY reuse of this template.
        -->
        <mj-text css-class="meta" padding-bottom="24px">
          {{DATE_TIME}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        6d. TOPIC LINE
        HOW: "Topic:" in bold + the transformation, not the subject matter.
        -->
        <mj-text font-weight="600" line-height="1.7" padding-bottom="24px">
          <strong>Topic:</strong> {{TOPIC_LINE}}
        </mj-text>

        <!--
        6e. AGENDA — three bullets, no more
        HOW: recommended order, weakest to most desirable:
          Bullet 1 -> the ingredients / what a working version looks like
          Bullet 2 -> the speed or effort objection removed
          Bullet 3 -> your signature method, named, last
        -->
        <mj-text font-family="'Poppins', sans-serif" font-size="14px" font-weight="600" padding-bottom="14px">
          📌 Agenda:
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text line-height="1.85">
          <ul style="margin:0 0 0 18px;padding:0;list-style:none;">
            <li style="margin-bottom:12px;">{{BULLET_1}}</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom:12px;">{{BULLET_2}}</li>
            <li>{{BULLET_3}}</li>
          </ul>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    7. CTA #2 — THE CLOSE
    WHY: peak intent. Don't make them scroll back up to find a button.
    HOW: same URL, slightly different wording. On day 0, stop at two CTAs --
    add the third one in the reminder emails, where real urgency justifies
    it.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="32px 24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-button href="{{REGISTRATION_URL}}">
          {{CTA_SECONDARY}}
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section>
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ====================================================================
    8. FOOTER — LEGAL AND DELIVERABILITY
    HOW: do not touch the {webview_url} and {unsubscribe_url} tokens.
    ==================================================================== -->
    <mj-section padding="32px 24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-family="'Poppins', sans-serif" font-size="15px" font-weight="600" padding-bottom="8px">
          {{BRAND_NAME}}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="center" css-class="meta" padding-bottom="18px">
          {{POSTAL_ADDRESS}}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="center" css-class="micro" padding-bottom="14px">
          This email was sent to {contactfield=email}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px">
          <a href="{webview_url}" style="color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;">View in browser</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
          <a href="{unsubscribe_url}" style="color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;">Unsubscribe</a>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!--
    ==========================================================================
    PRE-SEND CHECKLIST
    - Both buttons point to the same URL, with UTM parameters.
    - Day, date and time match across subject, body and landing page.
    - The two quotes are REAL quotes from real people, not invented.
    - {contactfield=firstname|there} tested on a contact with no first name.
    - Subject line under 45 characters, preheader extends it.
    - No urgency language you'll need again in the reminder emails.
    ==========================================================================
    -->

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
